  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1233 PM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nRain comes to an end Tuesday night as the front and associated mid \nlevel trough push eastward. The air mass behind the front has spent \nthe last several days modifying over the desert southwest, so it \nwon't be appreciably cold by the time it gets here. However, we will \nsee temperatures some 10 degrees cooler for highs on Wednesday \ncompared to ahead of the front on Tuesday. Additional mostly dry \ncold fronts later in the week provide modestly better shots of \ncolder air, but not extreme by seasonal standards. In fact, by this \nweekend NBM probability of freezing temperatures increases to 10 to \n40 percent across the region, favoring the colder rural valley \nlocations. Nearly all locations in our forecast area are well behind \ntheir average first freeze, so if we are able to get a clear, calm \nnight in a cold air mass we could finally see that occur.",
